## 2. Source-readiness gap: the normaliser binds the host by prefix, not by parsed authority

The observation normaliser accepts a `tailapp.url.observed` record only when the lower-cased URL starts with scheme plus the supplied host (`tailapps/url-reputation/folds/normalize.jsonata@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c:19` builds the prefix, `tailapps/url-reputation/folds/normalize.jsonata@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c:26` compares it) and the character after that prefix is empty, `/`, `:`, `?` or `#` (`tailapps/url-reputation/folds/normalize.jsonata@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c:27` to `:28`). The colon is admitted so that a port can follow, but the check never parses the authority, so userinfo (`user:pw@`) before the real host is invisible to it. The existing boundary test covers only a userinfo spoof without a colon (`tailapps/url_reputation_test.go@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c:143`).

Bounded diagnostic, run through the real evaluator with the fixture and helpers of `tailapps/url_reputation_test.go@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c` (loadURLReputation, cloneURLInput, setURLAttributes, normalizeURLFixture) in a scratch checkout at this head:

| Case | observed_full | supplied host | Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| userinfo, correct host | `https://user:pw@example.com/path` | example.com | rejected (ineffective, 0 events) |
| userinfo spoof with colon | `https://example.com:pw@evil.test/path` | example.com | admitted (effective, 1 event) |
| same spoof, true host | `https://example.com:pw@evil.test/path` | evil.test | rejected |
| port then userinfo | `https://example.com:8443@evil.test/path` | example.com | admitted |
| control | `https://example.com/path` | example.com | admitted |

Both predictions in the assert are confirmed, and two more follow. A capture adapter that does what the decision requires, emitting the exact URL with its correctly parsed host (`notes/2026-08-31-url-reputation-stage-1-decisions.md@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c:24`, `notes/2026-08-31-url-reputation-stage-1-decisions.md@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c:34`), has its observation silently dropped whenever the URL carries userinfo, and there is no host value at all that the normaliser will accept for such a URL. Conversely a wrong host is bound to a URL whose real host is different whenever the supplied host is followed by a colon in the authority. The normaliser's job is to validate the adapter's host claim against the URL; for URLs with userinfo it validates the wrong thing.

Consequences for Stage 3. The companion's exclusion checks run on `host` (`tailapps/url-reputation/README.md@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c:94` to `:100` show the enabled-exclusion query; built-in host rules at `tailapps/url-reputation/folds/pipeline.jsonata@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c:35` and `tailapps/url-reputation/folds/pipeline.jsonata@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c:59`), so a wrongly bound host would apply host-exact and host-suffix exclusions to the wrong site, and a dropped observation never reaches the companion at all. Neither is a trust-boundary crossing on its own, because the host comes from the operator's own adapter, but the validator's purpose is to catch exactly that adapter error, and the drop case loses real observations.

Required bundle correction, bounded. In `tailapps/url-reputation/folds/normalize.jsonata@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c` derive the authority as the substring after the scheme up to the first `/`, `?` or `#`; if it contains `@`, keep only the part after the last `@`; strip a trailing `:` followed by digits; compare the remainder to the lower-cased supplied host exactly. Keep `observed_full` unmodified in the stored row (`tailapps/url-reputation/application.sql@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c:35` keys on it), and do not weaken the host-shape rule (`tailapps/url-reputation/folds/normalize.jsonata@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c:20` to `:23`). Add the five cases above to `tailapps/url_reputation_test.go@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c` as accept and reject assertions. The recovery backport of the bundle sources merged at #3960 to #3983 no longer carries a normaliser copy at this head, so no second copy needs the edit. This is a source change to a bundled fold within the same stored runtime with unchanged table shapes; whether an installed url-reputation Tailapp continues or resets is governed by `docs/reference/resident-upgrade.md@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c` and is not inferred or authorised here. The Stage 3 companion should be built and tested against the corrected normaliser, so this correction belongs before or at the start of Stage 3, and an unconditional "two new script trees only" scope is no longer accurate.

