## 6. Conclusions

Architecture. Stage 3 adds two producers outside the engine and one bounded correction inside the url-reputation bundle's normaliser fold; no layer contract changes. Ingest, evaluator, projection, query and the bundle schema stand as delivered, and the Stage 2 fixture already models the companion's records. Stage 4 touches CLI setup defaults and catalog docs only.

Security. Order in the companion: due query, exclusion set rebuilt in code including the seven built-in symbolic rules plus enabled materialised rows, exclusions, scrub, deduplicate, one explicit provider call, fan-out. Scrub both outbound target URLs and the key-bearing provider request URL before any error string is recorded. Refuse when the provider or its eligibility confirmation is absent. The fake provider and loopback proof must emit a distinct provider value and service name so a fixture verdict can never satisfy a real due query. Never open transcript_path. The normaliser correction closes the host-binding gap so host exclusions apply to the site the URL actually names and correct observations are not dropped.

Simplification. Keep both scripts single-file with a documented stdin contract. Reuse the README's due and exclusion SQL verbatim. No cache beyond url_verdicts and no fourth provider. The normaliser correction is a few lines of authority parsing plus five test cases; do not add a URL library to the bundle.

